# Normalised so a diff is a diff. Without this the repository carries 68 files with CRLF
# and 197 with LF, which makes every whole-file change show up as every line changed on
# whichever machine did it.
#
# The renormalisation itself (`git add --renormalize .`) is deliberately NOT done here:
# it touches every file in the tree and belongs in its own commit, not inside an
# unrelated change.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Generated and vendored artefacts: not ours to reformat.
# `-diff` alone was the bug. It stops git showing a textual diff, but the file was still
# classified as *text*, so `core.autocrlf=true` checked out CRLF and the working copy stopped
# matching the index. Every clone then had a dirty `backend/sbom/central.cdx.json`, which
# fails the release gate's first check - so a fresh clone of a released tag could not pass its
# own gate. Found by cloning v0.1.0 and running the gate in it, which is the only way to see
# it: the tree this was written in is on Windows, where autocrlf is already doing what the
# attribute asked for.
#
# `-text` is the actual fix. It says the content is not line-ending-normalised, so git leaves
# the bytes alone in both directions.
backend/sbom/*.json -text -diff linguist-generated=true
firmware/test/point_vectors.inc -text -diff linguist-generated=true

# Binary. Listed explicitly because text=auto guesses from content, and a wrong guess
# corrupts the file in the index.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.sqlite binary
*.sqlite-wal binary
*.sqlite-shm binary
*.bin binary
*.elf binary
*.pyc binary
